<!--
  Allen & Heath Xone:K3: a Cadence profile from the online library (A208).

  SOURCE, and only this: the manufacturer's own MIDI documentation.
    Xone:K3 User Guide – Allen & Heath (print of the Allen & Heath support-centre user guide) (Allen & Heath, printed 2026-04-27), pages 8-9 (MIDI Controls), 10 (Global MIDI Channel), 13-16 (Latching Layers, Unit Maps, Factory Map), 17-19 (MIDI Implementation Default: Send), 21-22 (MIDI Conversion Table), 24 (Specifications: MIDI defaults)
    https://leisuretec.co.uk/cdn/shop/files/Allen_Heath_Xone_K3_User_Guide.pdf
    Xone:K3 Guida Utente (canonical location of the same guide on the Allen & Heath support centre; Italian edition URL; not readable by my tools, HTTP 403) (Allen & Heath)
    https://support.allen-heath.com/hc/it/articles/39744774067985-Xone-K3-Guida-Utente
    XONE:K2 User Guide, Publication AP8509 Issue 3 (the K3 Factory Map is stated to match the K2) (Allen & Heath Limited, 2018), pages 14-16, 19
    https://acueexpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/11/XoneK2_UG_AP8509_3.pdf
  No mapping file from any other application was read or used.

  status="manual": the message is the manufacturer's. Nobody has tried this map on the hardware
  yet. If a control does nothing, use Learn on that row and tell us at shlabs.contact@gmail.com.

  BEFORE YOU START: Unit Map 1 (Factory Map, loaded by default), global MIDI channel 15, Latching Layers OFF.

  CADENCE'S CHOICES:
    Allen & Heath's guide was read from a retailer's print of the support-centre page: allen-heath.com refused automated downloads. Its factory map works the same way as a Xone:K2's.

  LEFT OUT (no Cadence target): Top-row encoder push switches (notes E3 F3 F#3 G3 = 52-55): no Cadence target that fits a push on the filter encoder.; Bottom-row left encoder (CC20, push C#0 = 13): left free.; LAYER button (C0 = 12) and SHIFT button (D#0 = 15): left free. The guide says SHIFT is typically used as a shift key in the host.; All amber and green layer messages (CC22-CC69, notes in octaves 4-9): they are sent only when Latching Layers are on.

  A jog wheel that moves too fast or too slow: set its row to Fine, or invert it, in the dialog.
-->
<CadenceMidiMap name="Allen &amp; Heath Xone:K3" maker="Allen &amp; Heath" model="Xone:K3" match="xonek3" version="1">
